      "text": "\nYou are a fair and expert exam evaluator.\n\nYou are given one student's handwritten answer (as images) for a specific question.\n\nThis question has multiple official sample solutions, and each sample has its own rubric.\n\nYour tasks are:\n1. Analyze the student’s answer.\n2. Decide which sample solution (from the list below) the student’s work most closely matches.\n3. Apply *only that sample’s rubric* to evaluate the student’s performance.\n4. Award marks per criterion, give feedback per criterion, and compute the total score.\n5. Be generous in partial credit for correct reasoning.\n6. If the handwriting or answer is blank/unreadable, give minimal marks and explain.\n\nReturn STRICTLY valid JSON (no markdown, no commentary) structured as:\n{\n  \"question_number\": 1,\n  \"qid\": \"1759693938216-0\",\n  \"used_sample_index\": <number | null>,\n  \"criteria\": [\n    { \"criterion\": \"<text>\", \"obtained_marks\": <number>, \"max_marks\": <number>, \"feedback\": \"<text>\" }\n  ],\n  \"suggestedScore\": <number>,\n  \"feedback\": \"<overall feedback>\"\n}\n\n---\n\nQUESTION:\nIf $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi]$ then determine the rank of matrix $M = \\begin{pmatrix} \\cos \\theta & \\sin \\theta & 0 \\\\ \\sin \\theta & \\cos \\theta & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}$.\n\nTOTAL MARKS: 4\n\nAVAILABLE SAMPLES (each has its own rubric):\n\nSAMPLE 1\nInstructions: please make a step by step solution for this. as a student would write in an exam. i have provided the image that contained right solution.\nAnswer:\nTo determine the rank of the matrix $M$, we first calculate its determinant. The rank of a square matrix is its dimension if its determinant is non-zero. If the determinant is zero, the rank is less than its dimension.\n\n**Given matrix:**\n$M = \\begin{pmatrix} \\cos \\theta & \\sin \\theta & 0 \\\\ \\sin \\theta & \\cos \\theta & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}$\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the determinant of M.**\nWe expand the determinant along the third row (or third column) as it contains two zero elements, simplifying the calculation:\n$\\text{det}(M) = 0 \\cdot C_{31} + 0 \\cdot C_{32} + 1 \\cdot C_{33}$\nwhere $C_{33}$ is the cofactor of the element at position (3,3). The minor $M_{33}$ is:\n$M_{33} = \\text{det} \\begin{pmatrix} \\cos \\theta & \\sin \\theta \\\\ \\sin \\theta & \\cos \\theta \\end{pmatrix}$\n$M_{33} = (\\cos \\theta)(\\cos \\theta) - (\\sin \\theta)(\\sin \\theta)$\n$M_{33} = \\cos^2 \\theta - \\sin^2 \\theta$\nUsing the double-angle identity, $\\cos(2\\theta) = \\cos^2 \\theta - \\sin^2 \\theta$, we get:\n$M_{33} = \\cos(2\\theta)$\nSince $C_{33} = (-1)^{3+3} M_{33} = M_{33}$, the determinant of M is:\n$\\text{det}(M) = 1 \\cdot \\cos(2\\theta) = \\cos(2\\theta)$\n\n**Step 2: Determine the conditions for the rank based on the determinant.**\nThe matrix M is a 3x3 matrix. Its rank is 3 if and only if its determinant is non-zero.\n\n**Case 1: If $\\text{det}(M) \\neq 0$.**\nThis occurs when $\\cos(2\\theta) \\neq 0$.\nGiven that $\\theta \\in [0, 2\\pi]$, the range for $2\\theta$ is $[0, 4\\pi]$.\n$\\cos(2\\theta) = 0$ when $2\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{3\\pi}{2}, \\frac{5\\pi}{2}, \\frac{7\\pi}{2}$"
